          ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular: **True.** This holds because all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **True.** This holds because all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${A}^{T}+A$ is lower triangular: **True.** This holds because the result of $A+{A}^{T}$ has all the entries above the main diagonal equal to zero: \n\n$$\n{A}^{T}+A=\\begin{bmatrix}16 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular.\n- $A$ is lower triangular.\n- ${A}^{T}+A$ is lower triangular."
