# Instructional account and repair scope

The learner must inspect each strict off-diagonal region, transpose when requested, and (at hard difficulty) add or subtract mirrored entries before deciding each statement independently. Upper triangular means every entry below the diagonal is zero; lower triangular means every entry above is zero. Tutorial 658a47dc-4d32-5d9d-a04c-82d683e87739 explicitly allows any number, including zero, in the unrestricted region and on the diagonal. Therefore a source example's qualifying label or zero-region assignment is not a constraint.

Source q-42091 (39d12d09-6555-5993-ad4c-5e191be1b0c7) and q-126479 (f41ff7d0-b754-5033-a620-53eef8a376e3) demonstrate lower-only and diagonal matrices with the same identity/transpose workload. q-126484 tests transpose lower rather than transpose upper. q-74318, q-74319 and q-126481 (5fc95051-8b70-5447-aece-290d3854c40e) preserve this method in observed 3x3/4x4 sizes. Hard q-126477 and q-42116 use transpose differences; q-13771, q-68754, q-42115 and q-126474 (814b1f0e-0432-56a4-8a3b-10efb7462756) use sums, including cancellation. Canonical example 205d32a2-ac26-5eaf-896a-c6182a70eff7 explicitly computes the transpose difference before testing the region. Prerequisite topic 6197c039-5830-56a2-b171-eac0f7516ad1 defines transpose by interchanging rows and columns.

Response contract: three full-statement Boolean checkbox fields; a visible None of the above is true exactly when all ordinary statements are false. q-42115 and q-42116 supply current checkbox None evidence. Replay preserves each supplied complete bank, field order, original difficulty (including q-42115's missing label), prompt and solution at original parameters. Normal generation carries None throughout this family so all-false cases remain selectable. No radio conversion is used. The historical packaged basis-1356 radio capture is retained as historical-source.json; the runtime capture is replaced by the supplied basis-5452 material. The newer source corrects the old referent errors. It contains 12 cases rather than 10; no source question is removed.

Fixed features and reasons: square matrices are required for triangularity; each source template retains its observed 3x3 or 4x4 size and its three expressions to preserve workload. Integer inputs -8..8 bound arithmetic to the observed scale. Diagonal entries are unrestricted within that range because they cannot affect triangularity. Operations and labels remain source-specific to preserve fidelity, but their truth patterns vary within every template. Moderate has identity plus transpose; hard adds exactly one observed sum/difference. Easy retains the prior authored 3x3 identity upper/lower/diagonal family, a conservative prerequisite-level extension. All three bands are supported; requested moderate is unchanged. No diagrams occur.

Construction chooses the answer-bearing region/cancellation case before numbers: diagonal, upper-only, lower-only, neither; hard additionally chooses nontrivial mirrored cancellation. For a sum, cancellation uses opposite mirrored entries; for a difference, equal mirrored entries. Noncancellation uses an explicit unequal pair. Nonzero support locations and magnitudes vary after the case; all keys, proof matrices and witnesses derive from the actual matrix. These are conservative same-method extensions of the lesson definitions, not additional source observations. Moderate must cover all four truth patterns per template; hard must cover diagonal, both one-sided cases, neither with cancellation and neither without it. A changed off-diagonal entry must change relevant truths; changing only diagonal entries must preserve every truth. Zero matrices and symmetric/skew off-diagonal cases are valid simplifications, not rejected samples.

The repair removes two design restrictions: source truth-vector/zero-region locking and the obsolete five-option radio-bank intermediary. Neither was instructional. Tests inspect visible matrix entries and statement text independently, including solution matrices, complete source replay, exact reported counterexamples, and conditional label/dimension/wording/position/count shortcuts before and after the shared delivery filter. Semantic counts use distinct matrices of zero/nonzero regions and cancellation, never UUIDs or seeds. Live learner history/weights are unavailable; only captured inventory filtering and read-only selection rules can be assessed.


